## Context
tabulate_self_consistency.py reads a pre-computed self_consistency_summary.json
with aggregate stats (majority_f1, union_f1, vote counts). This is a derived
analysis that should be computed on the fly from the individual RunRecords in
measurements.jsonl — group by model, merge the 3 runs, calculate votes at
render time. This eliminates the intermediate JSON file and brings the script
in line with the other reporting scripts.

## Actions
1. Add vote computation logic (majority/union) to tabulate_self_consistency.py.
2. Rewrite to read measurements.jsonl via shared loader.
3. Delete self_consistency_summary.json generation path.
4. Verify LaTeX output unchanged.

## Test
Generate table from measurements.jsonl and diff against current output from
self_consistency_summary.json — must be identical.

## Exit criteria
- tabulate_self_consistency.py reads measurements.jsonl, not summary JSON
- Vote computation (majority, union) done at render time
- self_consistency_summary.json no longer generated or required
- LaTeX output unchanged
- All tests pass
